mx-viewer (26.09) mx; urgency=medium

  * New tabs open a start page with your bookmarks and most visited sites.
  * Pin a tab from its right-click menu to keep it as a small icon at the
    left of the tab bar, safe from "close other tabs".
  * Open a private window (Ctrl+Shift+N) that saves no history, tabs or
    site data.
  * Reader view (F9) shows an article's text without ads and clutter.
  * Right-click a tab to reload, duplicate, pin, mute or close it, or to
    close other tabs; tabs playing sound show a speaker button to mute them.
  * Zoom level is remembered for each site.
  * Find in page shows how many matches there are and can match case.
  * Clear browsing data lets you choose a time range, such as the last hour.
  * Save a page or print it from the menu.
  * Right-click selected text to search the web for it.
  * Spelling mistakes are underlined in text boxes when spelling
    dictionaries are installed.
  * Sites must ask before using your camera, microphone, screen or location.
  * Warn about sites with certificate problems, with an option to continue
    anyway.
  * Ask for a user name and password when a site or proxy requires one,
    with an option to remember the password in the system keyring.
  * Videos and pages can go full screen.
  * When a tab crashes, show a page with a Reload link instead of a blank tab.
  * Links opened from other applications open as new tabs in the window
    that is already running.
  * Opening several files at once from the file manager now opens all of them.
  * Popup windows open as tabs and close again when the page is done
    with them.
  * New keyboard shortcuts: F6 or Alt+D to go to the address bar and
    Ctrl+PgUp/PgDn to switch tabs; the menu has a list of all shortcuts.
  * Tabs are shown in the title bar, with minimize, maximize and close
    buttons; drag the tab row to move the window. A setting brings back
    the system title bar.
  * Tabs all have the same width and shrink together when the row is full;
    the "+" new tab button is always visible.
  * Bookmarks bar under the toolbar (Ctrl+Shift+B): drag the address or a
    link onto it to add a bookmark, drag bookmarks to reorder them, and
    right-click one to open it in a new tab, edit or delete it.
  * History is listed newest first under day headings, with the time of
    each visit, and is stored in a database so large histories stay fast.
  * Redesigned About and Keyboard shortcuts dialogs.
  * Ask before closing a window while downloads are in progress.
  * Printing to a file saves to the Downloads folder, named after the page.
  * Reader view is kept when going back and forward.
  * Various fixes: the Home, Back, Forward and Stop buttons now work in
    every tab, menu and toolbar icons stay visible on dark themes,
    middle-clicking a link no longer leaves an empty tab, bookmark titles
    with "&" show correctly, and a possible crash when quitting is gone.
  * Web pages can no longer change your settings or clear your history.
  * When started as root, also give up root's group memberships.

 -- Adrian <adrian@mxlinux.org>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 13:12:28 -0400

